\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Construct on a $16\times 13$ instance, with the deleted lines shaded. The least endpoint $x$-coordinate is $5$, so SelectBlock returns the top block of two lines, rows $0$ and $1$. The $14\times 13$ instance that remains admits no block, and distant-endpoint compressions delete its lines $x=5,6$, rows $7$ and $8$ of the grid shown, and then the columns $y=5,6$. TableLookup solves the final instance, $12\times 11$ in the orientation shown (Algorithm~\ref {alg:construct} holds its transpose), by the template of Figure~\ref {fig:template}, where panel (b) shows the image of that instance on which the template checks. Band extension and EdgeSplice put the lines back, giving the solution shown.}}{17}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:example}{{10}{17}{Construct on a $16\times 13$ instance, with the deleted lines shaded. The least endpoint $x$-coordinate is $5$, so SelectBlock returns the top block of two lines, rows $0$ and $1$. The $14\times 13$ instance that remains admits no block, and distant-endpoint compressions delete its lines $x=5,6$, rows $7$ and $8$ of the grid shown, and then the columns $y=5,6$. TableLookup solves the final instance, $12\times 11$ in the orientation shown (Algorithm~\ref {alg:construct} holds its transpose), by the template of Figure~\ref {fig:template}, where panel (b) shows the image of that instance on which the template checks. Band extension and EdgeSplice put the lines back, giving the solution shown}{figure.caption.25}{}}
